The ﬁne-grained access control REST API diﬀers slightly depending on your OpenSearch/
Elasticsearch version. Prior to making a PUT request, make a GET request to verify the expected
request body. For example, a GET request to _plugins/_security/api/user returns all users,
which you can then modify and use to make valid PUT requests.
On Elasticsearch 6.x, requests to create users look like this:
PUT _opendistro/_security/api/user/new-user
{
"password": "some-password",
"roles": ["new-backend-role"]
}
On OpenSearch or Elasticsearch 7.x, requests look like this (change _plugins to _opendistro if
using Elasticsearch):
PUT _plugins/_security/api/user/new-user
{
"password": "some-password",
"backend_roles": ["new-backend-role"]
}
Further, tenants are properties of roles in Elasticsearch 6.x:
GET _opendistro/_security/api/roles/all_access
