{
"all_access": {
"cluster": ["UNLIMITED"],
"tenants": {
"admin_tenant": "RW"
},
"indices": {
"*": {
"*": ["UNLIMITED"]
}
},
"readonly": "true"
}
}
In OpenSearch and Elasticsearch 7.x, they're objects with their own URI (change _plugins to
_opendistro if using Elasticsearch)::
GET _plugins/_security/api/tenants
{
"global_tenant": {
"reserved": true,
"hidden": false,
"description": "Global tenant",
"static": false
}
}
For documentation on the OpenSearch REST API, see the Security plugin API reference.
Tip
If you use the internal user database, you can use curl to make requests and test your
domain. Try the following sample commands:
curl -XGET -u 'master-user:master-user-password' 'domain-endpoint/_search'
curl -XGET -u 'master-user:master-user-password' 'domain-endpoint/_plugins/
_security/api/user'
